# The Digital Ice Age triptych — CC BY 4.0

Three posts (the two already live, and Post 3 when it ships at Step 1). Each
carries the same footer, and the series as a whole carries the same license.

## 1. Footer for each post (Markdown)

Place at the end of each post, after the body and before any comments or
related-posts block:

```markdown
---

© 2026 Jason Doffing. *<Post title>* is part of the *Digital Ice Age*
triptych and is licensed under a
[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
(CC BY 4.0). Share it, quote it, translate it, build on it — just credit
Jason Doffing and link back to the original.
```

## 2. Footer for each post (HTML, with machine-readable markup)

```html
<footer class="license">
  <p xmlns:cc="http://creativecommons.org/ns#" xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/">
    &copy; 2026 Jason Doffing.
    <span property="dct:title"><!-- Post title --></span> is part of the
    <em>Digital Ice Age</em> triptych and is licensed under
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license"
       target="_blank">CC BY 4.0</a>.
    Attribution: <span property="cc:attributionName">Jason Doffing</span>,
    <a property="cc:attributionURL" href="<!-- canonical post URL -->">original post</a>.
  </p>
</footer>
```

## 3. If the posts live in a repository

Add `../cc-by-4.0/LICENSE` to the repository root (or to the directory holding
the posts, as `LICENSE`), and this line to the README:

```markdown
## License

The posts in this repository are © 2026 Jason Doffing and licensed under
[CC BY 4.0](LICENSE). Code samples inside the posts, if any, are additionally
available under the [Apache License 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
```

The second sentence is optional; include it only if the posts contain code
you expect people to lift. CC BY is awkward for code (attribution in a
compiled binary), so dual-offering the snippets under Apache 2.0 removes that
friction.

## 4. Site-wide line (optional)

If arops.dev or jasondoffing.com has a global footer, this replaces per-post
notices for everything under it. Keep the per-post footer on the triptych
regardless, since those posts get reposted.

```
Unless otherwise noted, writing on this site is © Jason Doffing and licensed
under CC BY 4.0. Code is licensed under Apache 2.0.
```
